    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73906" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμοφων-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>speak the same language with,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.142
			</span></i> : abs., <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				1.1.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>sound together</i> or <i>in unison,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				41.58
			</span></i> : c. dat., <i>sound like,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				7.25
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. τῷ λόγῳ</span>
			<i>chimes in</i> with . . , <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1102b28
			</span></i> ; <i>agree,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Them.
					<u>Or.</u>
					21.258b
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>P.</u>
					2.32
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>proclaim in unison,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑλλὰς δ᾽ ἀρετὰν ὁμοφωνεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Delph.</u>
					3(1).509
				</span></i>
			.</div>
